From: Devesh Rai <devesh.rai@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:20:04 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 41/46] Android: dialogs fit between the system bars; wizard
 caption; Ohm-metre dot
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

DIALOG_SHIM fitted dialogs on Android into the top-level frame's screen
rect.  The frames are maximized edge to edge, so that rect includes the
status bar and the navigation bar or taskbar, and tall dialogs (Plot,
Symbol Properties) opened with their top under the status bar and their
buttons cut off.  KIPLATFORM::UI::GetUsableScreenRect() gives the frame's
rect less its QWindow's safe area margins; the dialog's size and minimum
size are capped to that and the dialog is centred in it.

The startup wizard set its style to wxRESIZE_BORDER alone, which drops
wxCAPTION and wxCLOSE_BOX from wxDEFAULT_DIALOG_STYLE: a window without a
title bar on any platform that honours the style.  Add the flag to the
existing style instead.

Android's system fonts have no U+22C5 DOT OPERATOR, so "Ω⋅m" in the
calculator showed an empty box.  Use U+00B7 MIDDLE DOT there on Android.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
